# Accepted exceptions to the two Trivy Gates: the image Gate (job image-gate
# in .github/workflows/pr.yml, and the image job in release.yml) and the IaC
# Gate (job iac-gate, through scripts/check-iac.sh). Trivy skips every ID listed
# here, one per line: a vulnerability ID, or a misconfiguration check ID.
#
# This file is empty on purpose: every HIGH or CRITICAL finding blocks the PR
# until it is fixed. Fixing means a dependency or base image update, or a
# change to the Dockerfile or the chart, not an entry here.
#
# An entry is added only when a finding cannot be fixed yet, or is a
# deliberate choice, and only with a comment directly above it that gives both:
#   1. the justification: why it cannot be fixed now, for example no fixed
#      version exists yet, or the fix needs a breaking upgrade; or, for a
#      misconfiguration, why the flagged setting is what this app needs;
#   2. the reason it is safe: why the vulnerable code cannot be reached or
#      exploited in this image, or why the setting opens no way in.
# An entry without both is not merged. Remove the entry in the PR that ships
# the fix.
#
# Format (examples, not real entries):
#   # CVE-2099-0001 in example-lib 1.2.3. Justification: no fixed version yet.
#   # Safe because: the app never calls the vulnerable parser.
#   CVE-2099-0001
#   # KSV-9999 on Deployment example. Justification: the app must write to /x.
#   # Safe because: /x is an emptyDir that holds no code and is never executed.
#   KSV-9999
